# CrewSigningVectors — pinned cross-language ML-DSA-65 vectors for the crew production suite

These are the byte-verbatim outputs of the REAL `fips204` v0.4.6 crate, generated by the
`crew-kat-gen` harness whose complete source is reproduced at the bottom of this file.  The crew
kernel's production signing suite (`CrewFieldMission` — `ProductionSigning`) verifies these through
`Dregg2.Crypto.MlDsaVerifyReal.verifyCore`, the executable FIPS 204 verify whose own anchors are the
NIST ACVP `ML-DSA-sigVer` group (`MlDsaSigVerAcvp`) and the crate KAT (`MlDsaVerifyReal`).

Two-source discipline: the MESSAGES here are emitted by the Lean canonical signing-preimage
encoder over the kernel's own KAT world, the SIGNATURES by the Rust crate over exactly those bytes,
and acceptance is decided by the Lean verifier.  A drift in the encoder, the envelope split, the
context framing, or the verifier breaks the agreement loudly.

Provenance (reproducible):
* keygen: `ml_dsa_65::KG::keygen_from_seed(xi)` with
  `xi = b"POA-CREW-KAT-SEAT0-XI-SEED-0001!"` (seat 0) and
  `xi = b"POA-CREW-KAT-WRONG-XI-SEED-0002!"` (the wrong-key refutation pair).
* signing: `try_sign_with_rng` with the splitmix64 KatRng seeded `0x504f414500000001`
  (the hedge randomness only; outputs pinned verbatim below).
* signature contexts (FIPS 204 `ctx`): `"POA-CREW-SEAT-MLDSA65-1"` / `"POA-CREW-HANDOFF-MLDSA65-1"`,
  matching the kernel's `SEAT_SIGNING_CONTEXT` / `HANDOFF_SIGNING_CONTEXT`.
* the crate's own `pk.verify` was asserted in the generator: accepts each honest pairing, refuses
  the wrong-key/wrong-ctx/wrong-message pairings, BEFORE the Lean side ever saw the bytes.

⚠ These are TEST vectors for the KAT world only.  The seat-0 secret key is derivable from the
pinned xi seed by anyone; nothing deployed may ever use this keypair.
-/

